# Deny everything, then allow exactly what the image needs.
#
# An allowlist rather than a denylist on purpose: backend/.env holds a live
# app token, database URL, VAPID private key and Google refresh token, and
# backend/.venv is 356 MB. A denylist is one forgotten pattern away from
# baking both into a layer, and a layer that has held a secret keeps it even
# if a later layer deletes the file.
#
# "*" matches top level entries only, since Docker patterns do not cross "/",
# so re-including a directory below re-includes what is inside it.
*

!alembic
!alembic.ini
!app
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!uv.lock

# Anything the allowed directories might still be carrying.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
